### Backup Location
- Primary backups: `exports/backups/`
- Latest combined backup: `exports/all_dashboards_latest.ndjson`
- Working ESF backup: `exports/backups/macos_security_dashboard_working.ndjson`

### Restoration Command
If dashboards are accidentally deleted:
```bash
curl -X POST "http://localhost:5601/api/saved_objects/_import?overwrite=true" \
  -H "kbn-xsrf: true" \
  -u elastic:changeme \
  -F file=@exports/all_dashboards_latest.ndjson
```

### Important Notes
- Use legacy aggregation-based visualizations (metric, pie, histogram, table), NOT Lens
- Lens visualizations have strict API requirements and often fail programmatically
- Always test visualizations in the Kibana UI before committing changes
- Dashboard IDs are stable; visualization IDs should use the vis- prefix pattern
